  "modified": "2026-08-29T10:28:02Z",
  "details": "   * SECURITY UPDATE: local symlink attack through the unicast .local DNS\n     check: /etc/network/if-up.d/avahi-daemon exec's\n     /usr/lib/avahi/avahi-daemon-check-dns.sh as root, and the script\n     writes into /run/avahi-daemon (the checked_nameservers[.$$] cache and\n     the disabled-for-unicast-local tag) without protecting against\n     symlinks, so a local attacker able to place symlinks in that\n     avahi-owned directory can make root create arbitrary empty files or\n     cause a denial of service.\n     - debian/avahi-daemon.if-up: run the check script under\n       \"sudo -u avahi -g avahi\" instead of exec'ing it as root, so the\n       writes are performed by the same unprivileged account that owns\n       /run/avahi-daemon. Backported verbatim from Debian stretch\n       0.6.32-2+deb9u1 (DLA-3047-1); the alternative vendor fix, dropping\n       the check-dns mechanism outright (Debian buster 0.7-4+deb10u1,\n       Ubuntu focal 0.7-4ubuntu7), is not applicable here because bionic\n       ships libnss-mdns 0.10-8ubuntu1, the same generation as stretch.\n     - debian/control: add sudo to the avahi-daemon Depends, required by\n       the privilege drop.\n     - CVE-2021-26720",
